.TH VIRTIOMEM_CONVERT 1 "November 2026" "virtiomem_convert 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
virtiomem_convert \- convert libvirt domain XML configurations between virtio-balloon and virtio-mem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B virtiomem_convert
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR URI ]
.RB [ \-V
.IR VM_NAME ]
.RB [ \-b
.IR SIZE ]
.RB [ \-i
.IR SIZE ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR SIZE ]
.RB [ \-k ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-L
.IR WHEN ]
.I mode
.RI [ input_xml ]
.RI [ output_xml ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B virtiomem_convert
automates the modification of libvirt/QEMU virtual machine XML configurations to switch between traditional memory ballooning
.RB ( virtio\-balloon )
and modern block-based dynamic memory resizing
.RB ( virtio\-mem ),
and vice versa.
.PP
The tool can operate directly on offline XML files or update a defined domain in libvirt via
.BR virsh (1)
when the
.B \-\-vm
option is specified. All transformations are idempotent: running the command multiple times on an already converted configuration does not duplicate XML elements, but ensures the balloon parameters remain aligned.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I mode
Conversion direction. Must be one of:
.RS
.TP
.B to\-virtiomem
Converts the configuration to use
.BR virtio\-mem ,
configuring static base memory, NUMA topology, and the
.B virtio\-mem
device.
.TP
.B to\-balloon
Removes
.B virtio\-mem
devices, restores full static memory allocation, cleans up single-node NUMA definitions, and re-enables
.B autodeflate='on'
on the memory balloon.
.RE
.TP
.I input_xml
Path to the source XML file to read. Required when
.B \-\-vm
is not used; mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-vm .
.TP
.I output_xml
Path to the destination XML file to write. Required when neither
.B \-\-vm
nor
.B \-\-dry\-run
is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BI \-c " URI" "\fR,\fP \-\-connect " URI
Libvirt connection URI passed to
.BR virsh (1)
(for example,
.I qemu:///system
or
.IR qemu:///session ).
.TP
.BI \-V " VM_NAME" "\fR,\fP \-\-vm " VM_NAME
Name of the libvirt virtual machine to modify directly via
.BR virsh (1).
The virtual machine must be in the
.B shut off
state, be persistent, and have no snapshots before running the command.
.TP
.BI \-b " SIZE" "\fR,\fP \-\-base\-memory " SIZE
Minimum guaranteed static base memory when converting with
.BR to\-virtiomem .
Accepts human-readable suffixes such as
.BR 1G ,
.BR 1536M ,
.BR 2GiB ,
or raw integer values in KiB. The value is rounded down to a multiple of
.B 2 MiB
(2048 KiB). Defaults to
.BR 1GiB .
.TP
.BI \-i " SIZE" "\fR,\fP \-\-initial\-memory " SIZE
Initial total guest memory. Uses the same units as
.BR \-\-base\-memory .
With
.BR to\-virtiomem ,
the domain must not already have a virtio-mem device. The value must be between
the fixed base and the selected maximum memory. If an explicit value is not a
multiple of 2 MiB, the converter rounds it down and reports the requested and
effective values on standard error. If omitted, the converter uses the
original
.B <currentMemory>
or falls back to
.BR <memory> .
.IP
With
.BR to\-balloon ,
sets
.B <currentMemory>
directly without 2 MiB rounding. The value must be positive and no greater
than the resulting
.BR <memory> .
.TP
.BI \-m " SIZE" "\fR,\fP \-\-max\-memory " SIZE
Override the maximum total guest memory. Uses the same units as
.BR \-\-base\-memory .
With
.BR to\-virtiomem ,
replaces the input
.B <memory>
as the requested maximum. The effective maximum is the aligned base plus
the capacity above it rounded down to whole 2 MiB blocks, regardless of
option order. For example, a base of 1024 MiB and a requested maximum of
2049 MiB produce an effective maximum of 2048 MiB. The domain must not
already have a virtio-mem device. If the initial memory exceeds the requested
maximum, supply a lower
.BR \-\-initial\-memory .
With
.BR to\-balloon ,
sets the output
.B <memory>
directly. If the initial memory exceeds the new maximum, supply a lower
.BR \-\-initial\-memory .
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep\-balloon
When converting with
.BR to\-virtiomem ,
leave the existing
.B <memballoon>
model unchanged instead of setting it to
.BR none .
If no balloon device exists, create a
.B virtio
balloon. This option is not valid with
.BR to\-balloon .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Simulate the conversion and print a unified diff of the changes to standard output without modifying the virtual machine or writing any files.
.TP
.BI \-L " WHEN" "\fR,\fP \-\-color " WHEN
Control ANSI color output for
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.I WHEN
can be
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
or
.BR never .
In
.B auto
mode (default), colors are enabled if standard output is connected to an interactive terminal (TTY), highlighting added lines in green, removed lines in red, and modified values within corresponding XML tags in bold blue.
.SH XML TRANSFORMATIONS
.SS Mode: to-virtiomem
.IP \(bu 2
Sets
.B <maxMemory slots='16' unit='KiB'>
to the maximum memory aligned to 2 MiB blocks.
.IP \(bu 2
Sets
.B <memory>
and
.B <currentMemory>
to the static base memory value
.RB ( \-\-base\-memory ).
.IP \(bu 2
If no NUMA cells exist, creates
.B <cpu><numa><cell id='0' .../>
with all static base memory. Otherwise, assigns the remaining base memory to
the first NUMA cell after subtracting the unchanged allocations of the other
cells. The conversion fails if no memory remains for the first cell.
.IP \(bu 2
Adds a
.B <memory model='virtio\-mem'>
device with a 2048 KiB block size, setting
.B <size>
to the difference between maximum and base memory, and
.B <requested>
to the initial total memory (see
.BR \-\-initial\-memory )
minus the fixed base, rounded down to a 2 MiB block.
.IP \(bu 2
By default, sets
.B <memballoon model='none'>
and removes its
.B autodeflate
attribute and
.B <stats>
element. The
.B \-\-keep\-balloon
option leaves the current model unchanged and ensures
.B <stats period='5'/>
is present when the model is not
.BR none .
.SS Mode: to-balloon
.IP \(bu 2
Removes all
.B <memory model='virtio\-mem'>
devices and sums their
.B <size>
and
.B <requested>
values into the static memory fields. The fixed memory base is the sum of
NUMA cell memory, if present; otherwise it is the original
.BR <memory> .
.IP \(bu 2
Restores
.B <memory>
to the total maximum memory, updates
.B <currentMemory>
to the fixed memory base plus the requested virtio-mem memory unless overridden
by
.BR \-\-initial\-memory ,
and removes
.BR <maxMemory> .
.IP \(bu 2
Removes the
.B <numa>
element if it contains a single cell, or updates cell
.B 0
in multi-node topologies.
.IP \(bu 2
Changes
.B <memballoon model='none'>
to
.B <memballoon model='virtio'>,
then sets
.B autodeflate='on'
and ensures
.B <stats period='5'/>
on the
.B <memballoon>
device.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any non-empty value, disables colored output when
.B \-\-color=auto
is active.
.TP
.B FORCE_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value (other than
.BR 0 ),
forces colored output even if standard output is not a TTY when
.B \-\-color=auto
is active.
.TP
.B TERM
If set to
.BR dumb ,
disables automatic color detection.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error (e.g., invalid memory format, missing
.B <memory>
tag, virtual machine not shut off, or
.B virsh
command failure).
.TP
.B 2
Command-line syntax or argument validation error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview conversion to
.B virtio\-mem
on a live domain definition with 2 GiB base memory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
virtiomem_convert to-virtiomem --vm ubuntu-server -b 2GiB --dry-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Apply
.B virtio\-mem
to an offline virtual machine using a specific system URI:
.PP
.RS
.nf
virtiomem_convert to-virtiomem --vm ubuntu-server -c qemu:///system -b 1536M
.fi
.RE
.PP
Revert a virtual machine back to standard
.BR virtio\-balloon :
.PP
.RS
.nf
virtiomem_convert to-balloon --vm ubuntu-server
.fi
.RE
.PP
Convert a standalone XML file and pipe colored diff output to
.BR less (1):
.PP
.RS
.nf
virtiomem_convert to-virtiomem vm_orig.xml --dry-run --color always | less -R
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR virsh (1),
.BR qemu-system-x86_64 (1)
